{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0GMH", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-section-normalization}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:284258aab7bb835b75139fc7263dbbcad0b30335ae80b757c932dfbfae564723", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis section is the analogue of\nMorphisms of Spaces, Section <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4342f491f3bd6703ad95c4592bfc56aab35d9aa54f3706a6b2334b7eb2b0acee", "unit_id": "tag:0GMH:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0GMH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$U \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$U$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0007": "$U$", "MATH_0008": "$Y$", "MATH_0009": "$Y \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0010": "$Y$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0013": "$|\\mathcal{Y}|$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-prepare-normalization}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-prepare-normalization}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cbd481405cbd9597a59aadc05a0851f2edecd229b790892a3dcb711b9a349133", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d2e534ded84ec70d47b37e1117f51e6230f598f527a3022231d5c4d24d9f24c7", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an algebraic stack. The following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> there is a surjective smooth morphism <MATH_0002> where <MATH_0003>\nis a scheme such that every quasi-compact open of <MATH_0004> has\nfinitely many irreducible components,\n<STRUCT_0003> for every scheme <MATH_0005> and every smooth morphism\n<MATH_0006> every quasi-compact open of <MATH_0007> has finitely many\nirreducible components,\n<STRUCT_0004> for every algebraic space <MATH_0008> and smooth morphism <MATH_0009>\nthe space <MATH_0010> satisfies the equivalent conditions of\nMorphisms of Spaces, Lemma <REF_0001>,\nand\n<STRUCT_0005> for every quasi-compact algebraic stack <MATH_0011> smooth over\n<MATH_0012> the space <MATH_0013> has finitely many irreducible\ncomponents.\n<STRUCT_0006>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ee0a273f2c215b244a691cf2d659ea6ea7819d3d7c6d920e0ffe6528725261fb", "unit_id": "tag:0GMI:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0GMH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{Y} \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$V$", "MATH_0004": "$V \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0005": "$V$", "MATH_0006": "$|V| \\to |\\mathcal{Y}|$", "MATH_0007": "$|\\mathcal{Y}|$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{descent-lemma-locally-finite-nr-irred-local-fppf}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{stacks-properties-lemma-type-property}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-prepare-normalization}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{stacks-properties-lemma-quasi-compact-stack}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{topology-lemma-surjective-continuous-irreducible-components}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d70cb5d47b322549d716ba3fa8a9dd26595b6fe9017d881052e890eff7ed4168", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c59fcbee16f04764415ccfff478cfb279539c0600686e1f400816fa9df6f4f94", "source_text": "The equivalence of (1), (2), and (3) follow from\nDescent, Lemma <REF_0001>,\nProperties of Stacks, Lemma <REF_0002>, and\nMorphisms of Spaces, Lemma <REF_0003>.\nIt is also clear from these references that condition (4)\nimplies condition (1). Conversely, assume the equivalent conditions\n(1), (2), and (3) hold and let <MATH_0001> be a\nsmooth morphism of algebraic stacks with <MATH_0002>\nquasi-compact. Then we can choose an affine scheme <MATH_0003> and a surjective\nsmooth morphism <MATH_0004> by Properties of Stacks, Lemma\n<REF_0004>.\nSince <MATH_0005> has finitely many irreducible components by (2) and since\n<MATH_0006> is surjective and continuous, we conclude that\n<MATH_0007> has finitely many irreducible components by Topology, Lemma\n<REF_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c72b6b3639c14f57889f7fcfeef6d6578a7497916b26a6fc4fe081889af58806", "unit_id": "tag:0GMI:proof"}
